From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the desk has tile memory for every monitor

A renderer's tile budget is sized from the screen its widget starts on.
The desk page starts on the host monitor and learns the others later,
so a ~40 Mpx desk, plus a tiling for each less dense monitor, runs on a
laptop's budget. Over it, cc evicts and re-rasters on every commit and
draws required tiles as solid color: the shell blinks.

- A widget shown on monitors asks for upstream's memory per screen
  pixel for every pixel of the page and of each monitor's tiling, at
  most a quarter of RAM (DomicileTileBytesFor).
- The commit carries it to the compositor, which raises its policy to
  it and never lowers it, so upstream's budget is a floor.
- --force-gpu-mem-available-mb is the budget: with it, a widget asks
  for nothing.
- CommitState's copy keeps the display regions and the tile memory.
  Without the regions there, every commit after the one that set them
  clears the monitors' tilings.

See cc/domicile/display_regions.h; the series is read for this by
scripts/test-the-desk-has-tile-memory-for-every-monitor.sh.
